# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 49-58 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 9 — CHAPTER 11, 2026-09-20; the one run): 49 on 11:22 (walking in His ways, cleaving), 50 on
# 11:23 (the dispossession), 51 on 11:24 (the borders), 52 on 11:25 (no man, the dread, "as He spoke"), 53-54 on 11:26-28 (the blessing and the curse — Re'eh's
# opening), 55 on 11:29 (Gerizim and Ebal), 56 on 11:30 (the mountains' place), 57 on 11:31, 58 on 11:32; EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by
# ch11_ink.SP_; the middot checked in MIDDOT.md before they were typed; the rows read before marked REREAD WHOLE. Chapter 6's form.
from ch11_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(49, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO WALK IN ALL HIS WAYS" (11:22) — WHICH ARE THE WAYS OF THE ALL-PRESENT? "THE LORD, A GOD MERCIFUL AND GRACIOUS" (EXODUS 34:6); "ALL WHO ARE CALLED BY THE NAME OF THE LORD SHALL ESCAPE" (JOEL 3:5) — HOW CAN A MAN BE CALLED BY HIS NAME? THE ALL-PRESENT IS CALLED MERCIFUL, BE YOU MERCIFUL; GRACIOUS, BE GRACIOUS (PSALM 145:8) AND GIVE FREE GIFTS; RIGHTEOUS (PSALM 11:7), BE RIGHTEOUS; KIND (JEREMIAH 3:12), BE KIND; "ALL WHO ARE CALLED BY MY NAME" (ISAIAH 43:7), "THE LORD MADE ALL FOR HIMSELF" (PROVERBS 16:4). The head row of piska 49 — THE IMITATION ({SP_(49, 1, "אלו", "הן", "דרכי", "מקום")} "these are the ways of the All-Present"; {SP_(49, 1, "אף", "אתה", "היה", "רחום")} "you too be merciful"): "His ways" the attributes of Exodus 34:6 (chapter 10\'s attributes the kin; Sotah 14a the docket\'s); the English\'s note on Joel 3:5\'s vocalization read; no code. Fresh in both files.')
srow(49, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND TO CLEAVE TO HIM" — HOW CAN A MAN GO UP TO THE HEIGHT AND CLEAVE TO FIRE? "THE LORD YOUR GOD IS A CONSUMING FIRE" (4:24), "HIS THRONE FLAMES OF FIRE" (DANIEL 7:9). RATHER: CLEAVE TO THE SAGES AND THEIR DISCIPLES, AND I COUNT IT AS IF YOU WENT UP AND TOOK IT — NOT IN PEACE BUT AS IF YOU MADE WAR AND TOOK IT, "YOU WENT UP ON HIGH, YOU TOOK CAPTIVES" (PSALM 68:19). The cleaving to the sages ({SP_(49, 2, "הדבק", "בחכמים", "ובתלמידיהם")} "cleave to the sages and their disciples"): chapter 10\'s cleaving (10:20 — Ketubot 111b\'s value "the scholars", the compile\'s effect) said again on 11:22; 4:24\'s fire the row\'s seat at chapter 4 (read there, reread whole here). REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(49, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'THE EXPOUNDERS OF LORE SAY: DO YOU WISH TO KNOW HIM WHO SPOKE AND THE WORLD WAS? LEARN LORE, FOR BY IT YOU KNOW HIM AND CLEAVE TO HIS WAYS. YOU HAVE DONE WHAT IS ON YOU, I TOO WILL DO WHAT IS ON ME: "AND THE LORD WILL DISPOSSESS" (11:23). ({SP_(49, 3, "למוד", "הגדה")} "learn lore"); 41:20\'s "I too" said again (there the rain, here the dispossession — the two answers of the chapter); the row cites 11:23 ahead (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(50, 1, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THE LORD WILL DISPOSSESS" (11:23) — THE LORD DISPOSSESSES, FLESH AND BLOOD DOES NOT. The head row of piska 50 ({SP_(50, 1, "מוריש", "ואין", "בשר", "ודם", "מוריש")} "dispossesses, and flesh and blood does not dispossess"): the hiphil\'s subject the ink measured (the LORD the subject the book\'s one seat). Fresh.')
srow(50, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"ALL THE NATIONS" — LITERALLY? "THESE" — ONLY THESE; WHENCE TO INCLUDE THEIR HELPERS? "ALL THESE NATIONS FROM BEFORE YOU": YOU INCREASE AND THEY DECREASE — "LITTLE BY LITTLE I WILL DRIVE THEM OUT" (EXODUS 23:30), "I WILL NOT DRIVE THEM OUT IN ONE YEAR, LEST THE LAND BE DESOLATE AND THE BEASTS MULTIPLY" (23:29): R. JACOB. R. ELAZAR BEN AZARIAH: IF ISRAEL ARE RIGHTEOUS, WHY FEAR THE BEASTS — "THE BEASTS OF THE FIELD ARE AT PEACE WITH YOU" (JOB 5:23)? WHY DID JOSHUA LABOR ALL THAT LABOR? BECAUSE ISRAEL SINNED, "LITTLE BY LITTLE" WAS DECREED. Little by little ({SP_(50, 2, "מנין", "לרבות", "את", "מסיעיהם")} "whence to include their helpers"; {SP_(50, 2, "אלא", "לפי", "שחטאו", "ישראל")} "rather, because Israel sinned"): E1 (the extension by "all" — checked) after "these" restricts; EXODUS 23:29-30\'S "LITTLE BY LITTLE" (chapter 7\'s find — the phrase\'s two seats) read as the run\'s condition: Joshua\'s labor from the sin — the compile\'s DATA (the conquest\'s pace). Fresh.')
srow(50, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND YOU SHALL DISPOSSESS NATIONS GREATER AND MIGHTIER" — GREATER IN STATURE, MIGHTIER IN STRENGTH; "THAN YOU" — YOU TOO ARE GREAT AND MIGHTY, BUT THEY MORE. R. ELIEZER BEN JACOB: AS ONE SAYS, SO-AND-SO IS A HERO AND THIS ONE A HERO, BUT THE FIRST MORE. ({SP_(50, 3, "גדולים", "בקומה", "ועצומים", "בכח")} "greater in stature and mightier in strength"). Fresh.')
srow(50, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "THAN YOU" — WHY AGAIN, WHEN "SEVEN NATIONS MORE NUMEROUS AND MIGHTIER THAN YOU" (7:1) IS SAID? IT TEACHES THAT ONE OF THE SEVEN PEOPLES IS GREATER AND HARDER THAN ALL ISRAEL — "I DESTROYED THE AMORITE BEFORE THEM, WHOSE HEIGHT WAS AS THE CEDARS" (AMOS 2:9). One of the seven ({SP_(50, 4, "שאחד", "משבעה", "עממים")} "that one of the seven peoples"): E10 (the repeated expression — checked; chapter 7\'s outside row, read there on 7:1\'s count and reread whole here); the ink: "than you" plural here, singular at 4:38 and 9:1 (computed). REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(51, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"EVERY PLACE WHERE THE SOLE OF YOUR FOOT TREADS" (11:24) — IF TO TEACH THE BORDERS, "FROM THE WILDERNESS AND LEBANON" IS SAID; WHAT THEN? EVERY PLACE YOU CONQUER OUTSIDE THESE IS YOURS. OR MAY THEY CONQUER ABROAD BEFORE THE LAND? "YOU SHALL DISPOSSESS NATIONS GREATER AND MIGHTIER" (11:23) AND THEN "EVERY PLACE": NOT THAT THE LAND STAY DEFILED WITH IDOLS WHILE YOU CONQUER ABROAD — ONCE YOU CONQUER THE LAND, YOU MAY CONQUER ABROAD. DAVID CONQUERED ARAM-NAHARAIM AND ARAM-ZOBAH BEFORE THE JEBUSITE BY JERUSALEM — THE ALL-PRESENT: THE JEBUSITE BESIDE YOUR PALACE YOU HAVE NOT DISPOSSESSED, AND YOU CONQUER ARAM? The conquest\'s order ({SP_(51, 1, "כל", "מקום", "שתכבשו")} "every place you conquer"; {SP_(51, 1, "משתכבשו", "ארץ", "ישראל", "תהו", "רשאים")} "once you conquer the Land of Israel you may"; {SP_(51, 1, "דוד", "עשה", "שלא", "כתורה")} "David acted not according to the Torah"): the two verses\' order read as the conquest\'s order (I12\'s kin — no code typed); DAVID\'S ARAM the run\'s counter-case (2 Samuel 8, 10 — the Samuel walk\'s); the commandments abroad by the verbal analogy "shall be" (11:24 / Numbers 34:6-7) — the English carries it in this row, the Hebrew in 51:2. Fresh (the first draft\'s mark "read before at chapters 1-3" corrected by the computed list — no earlier ledger names 51:1).')
srow(51, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'IF THEY CONQUERED ABROAD, WHENCE THAT WHAT LIES OPPOSITE IN THE SEA IS THEIRS? "FROM THE WILDERNESS AND LEBANON" — FROM THE WILDERNESS IS YOUR BORDER AND THE WILDERNESS IS NOT; IF YOU CONQUER IT, IT IS YOUR BORDER; "FROM THE RIVER, THE RIVER EUPHRATES" — LIKEWISE; "TO THE SEA" — THE SEA IS NOT YOUR BORDER, IF YOU CONQUER IT IT IS: "THE GREAT SEA AND ITS BORDER SHALL BE YOUR SEA BORDER" (NUMBERS 34:6). HENCE: "EVERY PLACE THE RETURNERS FROM BABYLON HELD, FROM THE LAND OF ISRAEL TO CHEZIB — NOT EATEN AND NOT WORKED; THE RETURNERS FROM EGYPT — EATEN BUT NOT WORKED; BEYOND — EATEN AND WORKED" (MISHNAH SHEVIIT 6:1). THE MOVING BORDERS ({SP_(51, 2, "ואין", "המדבר", "גבולכם")} "and the wilderness is not your border"; {SP_(51, 2, "כל", "מקום", "שהחזיקו", "עולי", "בבל")} "every place the returners from Babylon held"): I2 (the verbal analogy "shall be" with Numbers 34:6 — checked; the Hebrew\'s form here, the English\'s in 51:1); THE MISHNAH QUOTED BY NAME INSIDE THE SIFREI (Sheviit 6:1 cited in the Hebrew\'s own parenthesis — the answer sheet inside the spine; Gittin 8a the docket\'s) — the two ascents\' lines a DATA row for the borders\' cell (Numbers 34 by CALL). Fresh.')
srow(51, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'THE BORDERS OF THE LAND OF ISRAEL AS FAR AS THE RETURNERS FROM BABYLON HELD: THE ASHKELON JUNCTION, THE WALLS OF MIGDAL SHARSHAN, DOR, THE WALLS OF ACCO, THE HEAD OF GATON AND GATON ITSELF, CABRATHA, BETH ZENITHA, THE CASTLE OF GALILEE, QABYA OF AYATA, MATZYA OF ABATA, KAMUTA OF BIRYIN, PAHORTA OF YATIR, THE WADI OF ABTZEL, BETH ER, MARASHTA, GREAT LULA, THE FORT OF BAR SANGARA, MESAF SEFANTA, THE CHANNEL OF IYON, UPPER TARNEGOLA OF CAESAREA, BETH SUKKOT, YANKAT, REKEM OF HAGRA, TRACHONA OF ZIMRA IN THE BORDER OF BOZRAH, SAKKA AND HESHBON, THE WADI OF VERED, SAKUTA, NIMRIN, THE FORT OF ZIRZA, REKEM GAIA, THE GARDEN OF ASHKELON, AND THE GREAT ROAD INTO THE WILDERNESS. THE LIST ({SP_(51, 3, "תחומי", "ארץ", "ישראל")} "the borders of the Land of Israel"; {SP_(51, 3, "פרשת", "אשקלון")} "the Ashkelon junction"): some thirty-five names in Aramaic — the baraita of the borders (the Tosefta Sheviit 4:11; the Rehov inscription the English names — the earliest rabbinic text in stone), no citation in either file (asserted among the eleven): a DATA row, the borders\' cell owed the names (9b). Fresh.')
srow(52, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"NO MAN SHALL STAND BEFORE YOU" (11:25) — ONLY A MAN? A NATION, A CLAN, A WOMAN WITH HER SPELLS — "NO MAN SHALL STAND": NONE AT ALL. WHY THEN "MAN"? EVEN AS OG KING OF BASHAN, "ONLY OG KING OF BASHAN REMAINED OF THE REMNANT OF THE REPHAIM" (3:11). The head row of piska 52 ({SP_(52, 1, "אשה", "בכשפיה", "מנין")} "a woman with her spells — whence"; {SP_(52, 1, "אפלו", "כעוג", "מלך", "הבשן")} "even as Og king of Bashan"): "man" read wide and then for Og (3:11 the row\'s seat at the first sitting — read there, reread whole here); the ink: the clause\'s three seats (7:24, Joshua 1:5 — computed). REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(52, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE DREAD OF YOU AND THE FEAR OF YOU" — IF THEY DREAD, DO THEY NOT FEAR? THE DREAD OF YOU ON THE NEAR, THE FEAR OF YOU ON THE FAR: "WHEN ALL THE KINGS OF THE AMORITES BEYOND THE JORDAN WESTWARD AND ALL THE KINGS OF THE CANAANITES BY THE SEA HEARD … THEIR HEART MELTED" (JOSHUA 5:1); RAHAB THE HARLOT TO JOSHUA\'S MESSENGERS: "WE HEARD HOW THE LORD DRIED UP THE WATERS OF THE RED SEA BEFORE YOU … AND OUR HEART MELTED" (JOSHUA 2:10). WERE THE MEN OF JERICHO NOT GREAT AND HARD? "GO SEE THE LAND AND JERICHO" (2:1) — JERICHO WAS IN THE GENERAL AND WENT OUT: IT TEACHES IT WAS HARD AS ALL OF THEM; LIKEWISE PHINEHAS (NUMBERS 31:6), LIKEWISE MOSES (EXODUS 15:1) — WEIGHED AGAINST ALL. Near and far ({SP_(52, 2, "פחדכם", "על", "הקרובים", "ומוראכם", "על", "הרחוקים")} "the dread of you on the near and the fear of you on the far"; {SP_(52, 2, "יריחו", "בכלל", "היתה", "ולמה", "יצאת")} "Jericho was in the general, and why did it go out"): E10 (the two nouns read apart — checked); RAHAB\'S "THE WATERS OF THE RED SEA" the ink\'s find (Joshua 2:10 the phrase\'s other seat, 11:4\'s — computed): the run\'s receipt of the chapter\'s own sea; the particular that leaves the general named without a code (the registry\'s I8 not among the codes checked this sitting). Fresh.')
srow(52, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'LIKEWISE "DAVID SPOKE TO THE LORD THE WORDS OF THIS SONG … FROM THE HAND OF SAUL" (2 SAMUEL 22:1) — SAUL WAS IN THE GENERAL AND WENT OUT: WEIGHED AGAINST ALL; ASAHEL (2 SAMUEL 2:30); PHARAOH\'S DAUGHTER (1 KINGS 11:1) — HE LOVED HER MORE, AND SHE MADE HIM SIN MORE THAN ALL. ({SP_(52, 3, "שאול", "בכלל", "היה")} "Saul was in the general"). Fresh.')
srow(52, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL PUT" — WHY SAID? SINCE "THREE TIMES A YEAR SHALL ALL YOUR MALES APPEAR" (16:16), ISRAEL MIGHT SAY: WE GO UP TO WORSHIP — WHO GUARDS OUR LAND? THE ALL-PRESENT: GO UP, AND I GUARD WHAT IS YOURS — "NO MAN SHALL COVET YOUR LAND WHEN YOU GO UP TO APPEAR" (EXODUS 34:24): IF HE DOES NOT COVET IT WITH HIS EYES, HOW WOULD HE COME TO TAKE GOODS AND CATTLE? SO NAAMAN TO ELISHA: "LET THERE BE GIVEN TO YOUR SERVANT TWO MULES\' BURDEN OF EARTH" (2 KINGS 5:17) — IF HE FEARED TO TAKE EARTH FROM THE LAND WITHOUT LEAVE, HOW WOULD HE TAKE GOODS AND CATTLE? "AS HE SPOKE TO YOU" — AND WHERE DID HE SPEAK? "I WILL SEND MY TERROR BEFORE YOU AND CONFOUND ALL THE PEOPLE YOU COME AMONG" (EXODUS 23:27). THE RECEIPT\'S REFERENT NAMED ({SP_(52, 4, "עלו", "ושלכם", "אני", "שומר")} "go up, and I guard what is yours"; {SP_(52, 4, "והיכן", "דבר")} "and where did He speak"): I1 (checked) from Naaman\'s earth; THE SHELF POINTS 11:25\'S "AS HE SPOKE TO YOU" AT EXODUS 23:27 — the receipt by "spoke" (the register\'s seat, the finder\'s third form) given its callee by the teacher (the compile\'s RUN_CITATION with its why — 9b); the pilgrimage\'s guard (Pesachim 8b the docket\'s). Fresh.')
srow(53, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SEE, I SET BEFORE YOU TODAY A BLESSING AND A CURSE" (11:26) — WHY SAID? SINCE "LIFE AND DEATH I HAVE SET BEFORE YOU, THE BLESSING AND THE CURSE" (30:19), ISRAEL MIGHT SAY: TWO WAYS ARE BEFORE US, LET US WALK IN WHICH WE PLEASE — "AND YOU SHALL CHOOSE LIFE" (30:19). THE MAN AT THE CROSSROADS BEFORE TWO PATHS — ONE SMOOTH AT ITS START AND THORNS AT ITS END, ONE THORNS AT ITS START AND SMOOTH AT ITS END — WHO TOLD THE PASSERS-BY: THIS SMOOTH ONE ENDS IN THORNS, THAT THORNY ONE ENDS SMOOTH. SO MOSES TO ISRAEL: THE WICKED PROSPER TWO OR THREE DAYS AND END IN REGRET (PROVERBS 24:20; ECCLESIASTES 4:1, 4:5; PROVERBS 4:19); THE RIGHTEOUS SUFFER TWO OR THREE DAYS AND REJOICE AT THE END — "TO DO YOU GOOD AT YOUR END" (8:16), ECCLESIASTES 7:8, JEREMIAH 29:11, PROVERBS 4:18. The head row of piska 53 — RE\'EH\'S OPENING INSIDE THE CHAPTER ({SP_(53, 1, "שמא", "יאמרו", "ישראל")} "lest Israel say"; {SP_(53, 1, "משל", "לאחד", "שהיה", "יושב", "על", "פרשת", "דרכים")} "a parable of one who sat at a crossroads"): E26 (checked); 30:19\'s "choose life" the pair\'s teacher (the compile\'s case row: the blessing if / the curse if not, the choice commanded); chapter 8\'s row on 8:16 (read there, reread whole here). REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(53, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'R. JOSHUA BEN KORHAH: THE KING WHO MADE A FEAST AND SIGNALLED HIS FRIEND TO TAKE THE FINE PORTION, AND HE HAD NO SENSE — "I WILL INSTRUCT YOU AND TEACH YOU THE WAY" (PSALM 32:8); WHEN HE SAW HE HAD NO SENSE, HE TOOK HIS HAND AND SET IT ON THE FINE PORTION — "THE LORD IS THE PORTION OF MY LOT AND MY CUP, YOU HOLD MY LOT" (PSALM 16:5); ISRAEL THANK AND PRAISE THAT NO PORTION IS AS FINE AS THEIRS (16:6-7). ({SP_(53, 2, "אחז", "את", "ידו", "והניחה", "על", "מנה", "יפה")} "he took his hand and set it on the fine portion"); E26 (checked). Fresh.')
srow(54, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"A BLESSING AND A CURSE" (11:26-28) — THE BLESSING IF YOU HEARKEN, THE CURSE IF YOU DO NOT HEARKEN; LIKEWISE "IF YOU DO WELL, IT IS LIFTED" (GENESIS 4:7) — A BLESSING, AND IF NOT — A CURSE. R. ELIEZER SON OF R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: WHO WHISPERED IT TO YOU? THE TORAH SAID IT — "THE BLESSING IF YOU HEARKEN, AND THE CURSE IF YOU DO NOT HEARKEN"; LIKEWISE "DEATH AND LIFE ARE IN THE HAND OF THE TONGUE" (PROVERBS 18:21) — "GUARD YOUR TONGUE FROM EVIL" (PSALM 34:14); "THE RIGHTEOUS IS REPAID ON EARTH, HOW MUCH MORE THE WICKED" (PROVERBS 11:31) — "THE LORD MADE ALL FOR HIMSELF, EVEN THE WICKED FOR THE DAY OF EVIL" (16:4). The pair ({SP_(54, 1, "הברכה", "אם", "תשמעו", "והקללה", "אם", "לא", "תשמעו")} "the blessing if you hearken, and the curse if you do not hearken"; {SP_(54, 1, "מי", "לחשך")} "who whispered to you"): the verse\'s own "if" the Torah\'s (11:27-28 cited in the English); Cain\'s Genesis 4:7 the kin (read at gen_12 and reread whole here) — 45:1\'s verse again. REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(54, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE CURSE IF YOU DO NOT HEARKEN" (11:28) — WE LEARN THAT JACOB OUR FATHER CHARGED HIS SONS ONLY WHEN HIS DAYS WERE DONE, WHEN HE LEANED TO DIE, WHEN HE HAD SEEN ALL THE MIRACLES DONE FOR HIM; SO MOSES OUR MASTER REBUKED ISRAEL ONLY WHEN HIS DAYS WERE DONE — "AFTER HE HAD SMITTEN SIHON" (1:4). The rebuke at the end ({SP_(54, 2, "שלא", "צוה", "יעקב", "אבינו", "את", "בניו")} "that Jacob our father did not charge his sons"): 1:4\'s row at the first sitting (read there, reread whole here) — the book\'s opening read as the deathbed rebuke (piska 1\'s theme). REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(54, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND TURN ASIDE FROM THE WAY" — FROM THE WAY OF LIFE TO THE WAY OF DEATH. ({SP_(54, 3, "מדרך", "חיים", "לדרך", "מות")} "from the way of life to the way of death"); 43:15\'s words on 11:16 said again. Fresh.')
srow(54, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM THE WAY WHICH I COMMAND YOU TODAY, TO GO AFTER OTHER GODS" — HENCE THEY SAID: WHOEVER ACKNOWLEDGES IDOLATRY DENIES THE WHOLE TORAH, AND WHOEVER DENIES IDOLATRY ACKNOWLEDGES THE WHOLE TORAH. The rule ({SP_(54, 4, "כל", "המודה", "בעבודה", "זרה", "כופר", "בכל", "התורה")} "whoever acknowledges idolatry denies the whole Torah"): the Sifrei on Numbers 111\'s parallel (the note) — the compile\'s DATA (Sotah 37a\'s "the whole Torah" the docket\'s; the curse\'s content the turning to other gods). Fresh.')
srow(55, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IT SHALL BE, WHEN THE LORD YOUR GOD BRINGS YOU" (11:29) — "AND IT SHALL BE" IS AT ONCE; "WHEN HE BRINGS YOU" — TAKE ON YOURSELF THE COMMANDMENT SAID IN THE MATTER, FOR ITS REWARD YOU ENTER THE LAND; "WHICH YOU ARE ENTERING TO POSSESS" — FOR THE REWARD OF ENTERING, YOU POSSESS. The head row of piska 55 ({SP_(55, 1, "אין", "והיה", "אלא", "מיד")} "and it shall be is nothing but at once"; {SP_(55, 1, "בשכר", "שתבא", "תירש")} "for the reward of entering you possess"): "and it shall be" read as immediacy (the shelf\'s standing rule — the Sifrei\'s commonplace the English notes at 75, 156, 170); the ceremony\'s time the compile\'s DATA (Joshua 8:30-35 the run). Fresh.')
srow(55, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL SET THE BLESSING ON MOUNT GERIZIM" — WHAT DOES SCRIPTURE TEACH, THE BLESSING ON GERIZIM AND THE CURSE ON EBAL? IT IS SAID "THESE SHALL STAND TO BLESS THE PEOPLE ON MOUNT GERIZIM … AND THESE ON THE CURSE ON MOUNT EBAL" (27:12-13)! MIGHT ALL THE BLESSINGS PRECEDE THE CURSES? "YOU SHALL SET THE BLESSING": A BLESSING PRECEDES A CURSE, NOT THE BLESSINGS THE CURSES. AND TO LIKEN THE CURSES TO THE BLESSINGS: AS THE CURSES BY THE LEVITES, SO THE BLESSINGS; AS IN A LOUD VOICE, SO; AS IN THE HOLY TONGUE, SO; AS BY GENERAL AND PARTICULAR, SO; AS TO BOTH THESE AND THOSE ANSWER AMEN, SO — TURNING THEIR FACES AT THE BLESSING TO GERIZIM AND AT THE CURSE TO EBAL. THE CEREMONY\'S FORM ({SP_(55, 2, "ברכה", "קודמת", "לקללה")} "a blessing precedes a curse"; {SP_(55, 2, "מה", "קללות", "בלוים", "אף", "ברכות", "בלוים")} "as the curses by the Levites so the blessings"): the likening (hekesh) of the curses to the blessings named without a code; 27:12-13 cited by name (the chapter-27 ceremony by CALL at 9b — Mishnah Sotah 7:2-5, Sotah 32a-37b the docket\'s; the Tosefta Sotah 8:10 in the note): the alternation, the Levites, the voice, the tongue, the Amen — a DATA row. Fresh.')
srow(56, 1, 'CONTEXT', f'"ARE THEY NOT BEYOND THE JORDAN" (11:30) — BEYOND THE JORDAN AND ONWARD: R. JUDAH. The head row of piska 56 ({SP_(56, 1, "מעבר", "הירדן", "ואילך")} "beyond the Jordan and onward"). Fresh.')
srow(56, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"BEHIND THE WAY OF THE GOING DOWN OF THE SUN" — THE PLACE WHERE THE SUN RISES. ({SP_(56, 2, "מקום", "שחמה", "זורחת")} "the place where the sun rises"): R. Judah\'s reading of the sun\'s "entrance" as its rising (the English\'s "in the East"); 56:3 R. Eliezer\'s the setting. Fresh.')
srow(56, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"BESIDE THE TEREBINTHS OF MOREH" — AND THERE: "ABRAM PASSED THROUGH THE LAND TO THE PLACE OF SHECHEM, TO THE TEREBINTH OF MOREH" (GENESIS 12:6): AS THE TEREBINTH OF MOREH THERE IS SHECHEM, SO HERE. R. ELAZAR SON OF R. YOSE: I SAID TO THE SAMARITAN SCRIBES, YOU HAVE FORGED THE TORAH AND GAINED NOTHING, WRITING "BESIDE THE TEREBINTHS OF MOREH, SHECHEM" — WE TOO LEARN THAT THIS IS GERIZIM AND EBAL AMONG THE SAMARITANS, FROM GENESIS 12:6. R. ELIEZER: IT IS NOT THE GERIZIM AND EBAL AMONG THE SAMARITANS — "BEYOND THE JORDAN": NEAR THE JORDAN\'S BANK; "THE GOING DOWN OF THE SUN": WHERE THE SUN SETS; "THE CANAANITE": THEY WERE HIVITES; "IN THE ARABAH": THEY SIT AMONG THE HILLS; "OPPOSITE GILGAL": THESE DO NOT SEE GILGAL. THE MOUNTAINS\' PLACE — THE DISPUTE ({SP_(56, 3, "זיפתם", "את", "התורה")} "you have forged the Torah"; {SP_(56, 3, "הסמוכים", "לעבר", "הירדן")} "those adjacent to the Jordan\'s bank"; {SP_(56, 3, "אין", "אלו", "רואים", "את", "הגלגל")} "these do not see Gilgal"): I2 (the verbal analogy "terebinth of Moreh" with Genesis 12:6 — checked; the English\'s note names it); THE SAMARITAN TEXT\'S ADDED "SHECHEM" NAMED AS A FORGERY that changes nothing — a witness to a variant reading (the census\'s DATA); R. Eliezer\'s five readings of 11:30\'s clauses against Shechem (Sotah 33b-34a the docket\'s: the two mounds by Gilgal); GILGAL the Torah\'s one seat (computed). Read before at a Genesis sitting (gen_27 — the call, Abram at Shechem), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(56, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'R. ELIEZER BEN JACOB: THE VERSE COMES ONLY TO SHOW THEM THE WAY THE SECOND TIME AS THE FIRST — "THE WAY": WALK ON THE ROAD, NOT THROUGH THE FIELDS; "WHO DWELLS": IN THE SETTLED LAND, NOT THE WILDERNESS; "IN THE ARABAH": ON THE PLAIN, NOT THE HILLS. ({SP_(56, 4, "בדרך", "לכו", "אל", "תלכו", "בשדות")} "walk on the road, do not walk through the fields"): the verse read as a route (the English\'s "the second entry" — after the first under Joshua). Fresh.')
srow(57, 1, 'CONTEXT', f'"FOR YOU ARE CROSSING THE JORDAN" (11:31) — FROM YOUR CROSSING THE JORDAN YOU KNOW THAT YOU POSSESS THE LAND. The head row of piska 57 ({SP_(57, 1, "מעבירתכם", "את", "הירדן")} "from your crossing the Jordan"). Fresh.')
srow(57, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU" — BY YOUR MERIT. ({SP_(57, 2, "בזכותכם")} "by your merit"). Fresh.')
srow(57, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND YOU SHALL POSSESS IT AND DWELL IN IT" — FOR THE REWARD OF POSSESSING, YOU DWELL. ({SP_(57, 3, "בשכר", "שתירש", "תשב")} "for the reward of possessing you dwell"); the sages\' verse (80:4-5) the outside rows\'. Fresh.')
srow(58, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL KEEP" (11:32) — THIS IS MISHNAH; "TO DO" — THIS IS THE DEED; "ALL THE STATUTES" — THESE ARE THE EXPOSITIONS; "AND THE JUDGMENTS" — THESE ARE THE LAWS; "WHICH I SET BEFORE YOU TODAY" — LET THEM BE DEAR TO YOU TODAY AS IF YOU RECEIVED THEM TODAY FROM MOUNT SINAI, FLUENT IN YOUR MOUTHS AS IF YOU HEARD THEM TODAY. The chapter\'s last row ({SP_(58, 1, "זו", "משנה")} "this is Mishnah"; {SP_(58, 1, "אלו", "המדרשות")} "these are the expositions"; {SP_(58, 1, "כאלו", "היום", "קבלתם", "אותם", "מהר", "סיני")} "as if today you received them from Mount Sinai"): the four terms of the frame assigned to the four kinds of the oral shelf (the Sifra and Mekhilta parallels in the note; 48:10\'s midrash, laws and lore the kin); "today" the frame\'s word (11:26, 11:32 — computed; 12:1 reopens it). Fresh in both files.')

